hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16171","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, he said: I heard Amr ibn Maymun narrate, from Abdullah ibn Rabiah al-Sulami, from Ubayd ibn Khalid al-Sulami, and he was of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made brotherhood between two men. One of them was killed in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then the other died, so they prayed over him. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What did you say? He said: We said: O Allah, forgive him, O Allah, have mercy on him, O Allah, join him to his companion. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then where is his prayer after his prayer, and where is his fasting or his work after his work? What is between them is farther than what is between heaven and earth."
